1
00:00:15,660 --> 00:00:17,280
Forty-seven!

2
00:00:29,920 --> 00:00:32,280
And 50!

3
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:52,040
Out of 50 chops, I only
heard three good ones there.

4
00:00:52,580 --> 00:00:56,060
So far, that brings your total to 41.

5
00:00:58,140 --> 00:00:59,300
Sorry, Yu-Gi-Oh.

6
00:00:59,620 --> 00:01:03,840
Looks like the cereal water's
on you. Again. Oh, whatever.

7
00:01:04,160 --> 00:01:06,278
You got, what, 43 good chops so far?

8
00:01:06,540 --> 00:01:09,000
I'll catch up soon. Go on.

9
00:01:09,360 --> 00:01:11,580
It's your turn at the axe, Kirito.

10
00:01:12,340 --> 00:01:13,480
Yeah, in a sec.

11
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:18,717
Every day for the past
year and three months,

12
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:21,271
we've been hacking away at this darn tree.

13
00:01:22,520 --> 00:01:24,180
I can't take it anymore.

14
00:01:24,520 --> 00:01:26,638
There's no use complaining about it.

15
00:01:26,760 --> 00:01:30,977
Our calling's to cut the giga-cedar
down, so there's no getting out of it.

16
00:01:31,060 --> 00:01:33,236
Yeah, I know you're right, but still.

17
00:01:33,560 --> 00:01:36,148
It doesn't feel like
we're getting anywhere.

18
00:01:39,240 --> 00:01:40,660
That's its life now.

19
00:01:41,020 --> 00:01:42,457
What was it two months ago?

20
00:01:42,540 --> 00:01:47,460
I think it was at 235,590?

21
00:01:47,820 --> 00:01:49,300
I'm gonna be sick.

22
00:01:49,640 --> 00:01:53,934
After two months of chopping at it,
we only got its life down a lousy 50!

23
00:01:54,560 --> 00:01:57,060
It's gonna take us forever to cut it down!

24
00:01:57,860 --> 00:01:59,037
What do you expect?

25
00:01:59,120 --> 00:02:00,944
This tree's as strong as steel.

26
00:02:01,420 --> 00:02:05,620
Six generations of carvers worked
on it for 300 years to get this far.

27
00:02:05,960 --> 00:02:07,300
It'll get cut down.

28
00:02:07,720 --> 00:02:09,580
In 900 years or so.

29
00:02:09,880 --> 00:02:11,700
Oh, is that all?

30
00:02:13,320 --> 00:02:14,150
Well...

31
00:02:17,640 --> 00:02:18,880
What are you doing?

32
00:02:20,020 --> 00:02:22,196
You think you're such a smarty-pants.

33
00:02:22,400 --> 00:02:24,017
Why don't you use that big brain of yours

34
00:02:24,100 --> 00:02:26,457
to figure out how to
get us out of this job?

35
00:02:26,540 --> 00:02:27,377
Would you...

36
00:02:27,460 --> 00:02:28,520
Stop it!

37
00:02:29,500 --> 00:02:30,540
Get off!

38
00:02:31,860 --> 00:02:33,340
Now it's my turn!

39
00:02:33,780 --> 00:02:35,000
How'd you like that?

40
00:02:36,500 --> 00:02:38,220
Want more or do you give up?

41
00:02:39,060 --> 00:02:40,017
Not even!

42
00:02:40,100 --> 00:02:42,100
Hit payback time!

43
00:02:42,780 --> 00:02:43,920
No surrender!

44
00:02:44,320 --> 00:02:46,260
No, stop it! Nope.

45
00:02:47,080 --> 00:02:49,900
I knew I'd find you boys goofing off.

46
00:02:51,100 --> 00:02:52,020
Tonkii it.

47
00:02:53,700 --> 00:02:55,640
Oh, hi, Alice.

48
00:02:56,080 --> 00:02:58,677
Did your sacred arts
class let out early today?

49
00:02:58,760 --> 00:03:00,560
Cause, like, you're early.

50
00:03:02,200 --> 00:03:03,940
I'm not early at all.

51
00:03:04,140 --> 00:03:05,460
I'm right on time.

52
00:03:07,960 --> 00:03:10,136
Since you have the energy to wrestle,

53
00:03:10,840 --> 00:03:15,487
maybe I should tell old man Kirito to
add some more swings to your daily quota.

54
00:03:15,720 --> 00:03:16,780
No, not that.

55
00:03:16,960 --> 00:03:18,019
Anything but that.

56
00:03:18,280 --> 00:03:19,480
I'm just kidding.

57
00:03:20,380 --> 00:03:21,210
Here.

58
00:03:22,580 --> 00:03:24,480
It's time you had some lunch.

59
00:03:26,600 --> 00:03:28,080
It's so hot today.

60
00:03:32,160 --> 00:03:34,740
You better eat it fast before it spoils.

61
00:03:35,340 --> 00:03:36,170
Okay.

62
00:03:38,900 --> 00:03:41,120
The pie sure tastes good today.

63
00:03:43,240 --> 00:03:46,260
Alice, your cooking keeps
getting better. For real.

64
00:03:46,880 --> 00:03:48,400
Oh, I don't know.

65
00:03:48,760 --> 00:03:52,231
It turned out okay, I guess,
but it could have been better.

66
00:03:55,160 --> 00:03:56,180
You know what?

67
00:03:56,360 --> 00:04:00,713
If anything, I wish we could take our
time eating this instead of rushing.

68
00:04:00,840 --> 00:04:03,781
Why does food have to spoil
so fast when it's hot?

69
00:04:04,340 --> 00:04:05,400
Because it's hot.

70
00:04:05,600 --> 00:04:06,430
I know that.

71
00:04:06,513 --> 00:04:10,877
But in winter, we leave raw meat out and
it keeps for days as long as it's salted.

72
00:04:10,960 --> 00:04:11,790
Well, yeah.

73
00:04:11,873 --> 00:04:13,899
That's because it's cold in winter.

74
00:04:14,200 --> 00:04:15,030
That's right.

75
00:04:15,160 --> 00:04:19,395
And if we could keep food cold in
summer, too, it would last way longer.

76
00:04:20,420 --> 00:04:25,126
But to make it snow, you'd have to use
the forbidden weather-altering arts, too.

77
00:04:25,220 --> 00:04:29,691
Then an Integrity Knight from the Axiom
Church would come and take you away.

78
00:04:35,560 --> 00:04:37,260
Ice. That's it.

79
00:04:37,840 --> 00:04:39,360
Huh? Don't you see?

80
00:04:39,580 --> 00:04:42,237
If we had lots of ice, we
could keep the food cold.

81
00:04:42,320 --> 00:04:45,496
Then we could take our time
and enjoy Alice's lunches.

82
00:04:45,740 --> 00:04:48,280
I say we go have ourselves a quest.

83
00:04:48,700 --> 00:04:50,380
A quest for ice.

84
00:04:51,280 --> 00:04:53,460
Honestly, it's summer now.

85
00:04:53,720 --> 00:04:56,249
Where would you find
ice this time of year?

86
00:04:56,580 --> 00:04:58,800
Even the market at Senator is out.

87
00:05:07,040 --> 00:05:11,099
Wait, remember that story about one
of the village founders, Bercoli?

88
00:05:11,700 --> 00:05:12,800
Which story?

89
00:05:13,900 --> 00:05:16,920
You know, Bercoli and the
Northern White Dragon.

90
00:05:21,100 --> 00:05:24,276
He followed the Rural River
all the way to its source,

91
00:05:24,500 --> 00:05:26,477
the cave at the foot of the End Mountains.

92
00:05:26,560 --> 00:05:31,266
He went in and found a pile of treasure
with a big white dragon sleeping on top.

93
00:05:31,620 --> 00:05:36,208
Then, he grabbed a sword sticking out
of the treasure, and the dragon woke up.

94
00:05:38,600 --> 00:05:43,424
The story also says he saw giant icicles
a little ways past the mouth of the cave.

95
00:05:43,760 --> 00:05:45,340
I say we go and get them.

96
00:05:45,440 --> 00:05:46,440
That's crazy.

97
00:05:46,720 --> 00:05:48,100
That's not a bad idea.

98
00:05:48,400 --> 00:05:49,340
Wait, you too?

99
00:05:49,860 --> 00:05:51,957
Come on, you know the law of the village.

100
00:05:52,040 --> 00:05:52,870
It says we can't...

101
00:05:52,953 --> 00:05:53,783
Yes, I know it.

102
00:05:53,866 --> 00:05:55,937
It says kids aren't allowed
to play anywhere near the

103
00:05:56,020 --> 00:05:58,357
End Mountains unless they
have a grown-up with them.

104
00:05:58,440 --> 00:06:01,677
But if we're there looking
for ice, that's not playing.

105
00:06:01,760 --> 00:06:03,657
If our village had ice,

106
00:06:03,740 --> 00:06:06,937
all the food would last longer
and that would benefit everyone.

107
00:06:07,020 --> 00:06:10,697
So if we went to get some, it'd
be considered work, not play.

108
00:06:10,780 --> 00:06:12,197
She's right.

109
00:06:12,280 --> 00:06:14,057
It'd totally be work.

110
00:06:14,140 --> 00:06:18,697
Maybe but we wouldn't just be breaking
the village's law by going up there.

111
00:06:18,780 --> 00:06:20,517
We'd be breaking the other one too.

112
00:06:20,600 --> 00:06:21,437
What?

113
00:06:21,520 --> 00:06:22,977
Don't play dumb.

114
00:06:23,060 --> 00:06:25,017
The taboo index.

115
00:06:25,100 --> 00:06:27,300
No one's allowed to.

116
00:06:30,720 --> 00:06:34,367
You're right, but here's what
it says about the End Mountains.

117
00:06:34,580 --> 00:06:37,200
In book 1, chapter 3, verse 11,

118
00:06:38,180 --> 00:06:40,997
the index says none shall
cross the end mountains?

119
00:06:41,080 --> 00:06:42,904
that surround the human empire.

120
00:06:43,260 --> 00:06:44,260
By cross,

121
00:06:44,540 --> 00:06:48,977
it means entering the dark territory
on the other side of the End Mountains.

122
00:06:49,060 --> 00:06:51,884
It doesn't say anything
about going in the cave.

123
00:06:52,020 --> 00:06:53,940
Yeah, but...

124
00:06:54,620 --> 00:06:55,450
Ow!

125
00:06:55,533 --> 00:06:56,363
That settles it.

126
00:06:56,660 --> 00:06:57,757
This will be the end of the cave.

127
00:06:57,840 --> 00:07:02,140
weekend we'll find that dra
- I mean, find that ice cave.

128
00:07:02,440 --> 00:07:04,969
Okay, let's meet in
the morning at seven by

129
00:07:12,660 --> 00:07:13,517
the north gate.

130
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:16,617
You got it, and don't
oversleep. Oh, please.

131
00:07:16,700 --> 00:07:18,700
Making us carry everything.

132
00:07:19,020 --> 00:07:21,373
Who does she think we are, her servants?

133
00:07:21,580 --> 00:07:22,680
Stop complaining.

134
00:07:23,060 --> 00:07:25,317
Be happy we can still go
and do stuff with her.

135
00:07:25,400 --> 00:07:26,540
That'll end soon

136
00:07:27,500 --> 00:07:28,330
Why?

137
00:07:28,413 --> 00:07:30,617
She's the village elder's
daughter, that's why.

138
00:07:30,700 --> 00:07:33,937
She has to learn all that stuff
a lady's supposed to know.

139
00:07:34,020 --> 00:07:35,608
Like manners and etiquette.

140
00:07:36,080 --> 00:07:36,910
Yeah,

141
00:07:36,993 --> 00:07:39,057
and since she wasn't
given a calling like we

142
00:07:39,140 --> 00:07:41,857
were She has to study all
those sacred art skills,

143
00:07:41,940 --> 00:07:42,770
too.

144
00:07:42,853 --> 00:07:44,477
She's going to be a role
model for the villagers.

145
00:07:44,560 --> 00:07:47,197
That means no more playing
with us boys anymore.

146
00:07:47,280 --> 00:07:48,197
All right.

147
00:07:48,280 --> 00:07:51,339
What are the two of you
whispering about back there?

148
00:07:52,500 --> 00:07:54,760
Nothing Right? Right Right.

149
00:07:55,140 --> 00:07:57,357
We were just saying how
we'd get in trouble if

150
00:07:57,440 --> 00:08:00,146
we don't make it back
before the evening bell.

151
00:08:00,720 --> 00:08:01,960
Oh, good point.

152
00:08:02,980 --> 00:08:07,157
Then keep an eye on Solus, and when it's
in the middle of the sky, we'll head back.

153
00:08:07,240 --> 00:08:08,200
Come on, guys.

154
00:08:08,580 --> 00:08:09,800
Back to our quest!

155
00:08:19,660 --> 00:08:21,895
We're pretty far from the village now.

156
00:08:22,380 --> 00:08:26,920
Did you know back in the olden days,
back when Rulid was first founded?

157
00:08:27,520 --> 00:08:30,417
goblins and orcs came down
from the Dark Territory,

158
00:08:30,500 --> 00:08:33,577
raided the village and stole
a bunch of sheep and kids.

159
00:08:33,660 --> 00:08:36,137
Listen, if you're trying
to scare me, stop it.

160
00:08:36,220 --> 00:08:37,240
I know the story.

161
00:08:37,620 --> 00:08:42,032
An Integrity Knight came from Senator
and chased them all away in the end.

162
00:08:42,260 --> 00:08:43,090
That's right.

163
00:08:43,300 --> 00:08:44,460
And ever since,

164
00:08:44,800 --> 00:08:48,917
on clear days you'll see a Silver Dragon
Knight soaring above the End Mountains,

165
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:49,830
ever vigilant.

166
00:09:00,040 --> 00:09:02,580
We all saw that, right?

167
00:09:22,260 --> 00:09:23,217
It's the cave!

168
00:09:23,300 --> 00:09:25,420
We reached the Yen Mountains.

169
00:09:33,680 --> 00:09:35,020
Let's go in.

170
00:09:35,280 --> 00:09:37,340
It's why we came here after all.

171
00:09:40,080 --> 00:09:41,140
System Call.

172
00:09:41,400 --> 00:09:43,940
Generate Luminous Elements. Adhere!

173
00:09:55,480 --> 00:09:57,980
Well, I don't see any icicles yet.

174
00:09:58,400 --> 00:10:00,637
Didn't you say they were
supposed to be a little ways in?

175
00:10:00,720 --> 00:10:02,940
I don't know, did I? You did!

176
00:10:08,420 --> 00:10:09,340
Yu-Gi-Oh?

177
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:10,830
Yeah?

178
00:10:11,200 --> 00:10:13,788
Could you please bring
that light over here?

179
00:10:18,900 --> 00:10:19,730
Whoa!

180
00:10:21,700 --> 00:10:22,530
See that?

181
00:10:22,613 --> 00:10:23,443
It's colder now.

182
00:10:23,600 --> 00:10:25,247
You're right, it totally is.

183
00:10:25,440 --> 00:10:28,217
For a second there, I thought I
was coming down with something.

184
00:10:28,300 --> 00:10:31,717
It's kind of neat how it's winter
in here, but summer outside.

185
00:10:31,800 --> 00:10:33,976
I bet we'll find some ice further in.

186
00:10:34,260 --> 00:10:36,640
Yeah, hopefully not too much further in.

187
00:10:37,540 --> 00:10:41,481
What are we going to do if we happen
to come across a white dragon?

188
00:10:41,580 --> 00:10:43,600
We'll run away as fast as we can.

189
00:10:44,380 --> 00:10:45,340
Quit worrying.

190
00:10:45,780 --> 00:10:49,604
I seriously doubt it's going to
mind if we take a couple icicles.

191
00:10:51,160 --> 00:10:54,317
Hmm, it'd be neat if we could
grab one of its scales though?

192
00:10:54,400 --> 00:10:56,837
No, we are not doing that!

193
00:10:56,920 --> 00:10:57,900
Why not?

194
00:10:58,420 --> 00:11:01,773
How else are we going to prove
we saw a real live dragon?

195
00:11:06,680 --> 00:11:08,037
Look, it's ice.

196
00:11:08,120 --> 00:11:10,757
It's true, there's ice in here.

197
00:11:10,840 --> 00:11:14,000
And I bet you guys there's
even more up ahead!

198
00:11:22,400 --> 00:11:23,341
Do you see that?

199
00:11:45,040 --> 00:11:48,864
With this much ice, we can keep
all the food in the village cold.

200
00:11:49,100 --> 00:11:53,512
Heck, with this much ice, you can keep
the whole Tonkii village cold forever.

201
00:11:54,860 --> 00:11:56,897
Jeez, would you watch where you're going?

202
00:11:56,980 --> 00:11:57,810
Huchio, look.

203
00:11:59,880 --> 00:12:01,040
There it is.

204
00:12:02,900 --> 00:12:03,730
Whoa.

205
00:12:07,940 --> 00:12:08,920
The dragon?

206
00:12:09,580 --> 00:12:10,460
No way.

207
00:12:10,840 --> 00:12:11,880
How did it die?

208
00:12:15,880 --> 00:12:16,710
Look.

209
00:12:16,920 --> 00:12:19,120
Its claws all covered in gouges.

210
00:12:19,480 --> 00:12:21,540
And then it was chopped clean off.

211
00:12:21,800 --> 00:12:23,657
Then it must have fought with something.

212
00:12:23,740 --> 00:12:26,916
But I don't know of anything
that could kill a dragon.

213
00:12:28,680 --> 00:12:30,477
A sword made these marks.

214
00:12:30,560 --> 00:12:33,320
It's obvious what killed it. A human.

215
00:12:36,060 --> 00:12:36,890
But who?

216
00:12:36,973 --> 00:12:39,817
If a sword master like
Bercouli couldn't fight it,

217
00:12:39,900 --> 00:12:41,900
who'd be strong enough to kill it?

218
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:45,377
An Integrity Knight?

219
00:12:45,460 --> 00:12:46,520
But why?

220
00:12:46,940 --> 00:12:49,200
The White Dragons protect our realm.

221
00:12:49,460 --> 00:12:53,080
Why would an Integrity Knight
from the Axiom Church kill one?

222
00:12:53,840 --> 00:12:54,920
Wait a second.

223
00:12:55,200 --> 00:12:59,612
Maybe the Dark Territory has strong
knights too, and one of them killed it.

224
00:12:59,760 --> 00:13:00,980
If that's true,

225
00:13:01,120 --> 00:13:05,767
then the Armies of Darkness could easily
cross the End Mountains and attack us.

226
00:13:06,480 --> 00:13:08,080
Wait! What are you doing?

227
00:13:08,760 --> 00:13:10,880
This is heavier than it looks!

228
00:13:12,700 --> 00:13:15,420
Is that the sword? Yeah.

229
00:13:16,220 --> 00:13:18,760
The same one Bercouli tried to steal.

230
00:13:19,260 --> 00:13:21,220
The Blue Rose Sword.

231
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:31,320
It's too heavy.

232
00:13:31,720 --> 00:13:32,980
I can't lift it.

233
00:13:33,820 --> 00:13:37,400
Even with Eugeo's help, we'd
never carry this back to town.

234
00:13:38,640 --> 00:13:41,934
There's a bunch of other
treasure we could take, though.

235
00:13:43,960 --> 00:13:44,790
Mm-hmm.

236
00:13:44,873 --> 00:13:47,097
But something about
that doesn't feel right.

237
00:13:47,180 --> 00:13:49,200
It would be like grave robbing.

238
00:13:50,780 --> 00:13:52,717
Yeah, I guess you're right.

239
00:13:52,800 --> 00:13:54,100
We'll just take ice.

240
00:13:54,300 --> 00:13:55,888
The dragon won't mind that.

241
00:13:56,880 --> 00:13:57,880
How pretty.

242
00:13:58,380 --> 00:14:01,145
It's a shame it's just
going to end up melting.

243
00:14:01,620 --> 00:14:05,326
I couldn't care less as long as
it makes our meals last longer.

244
00:14:05,560 --> 00:14:07,857
Not just our meals, everyone's.

245
00:14:07,940 --> 00:14:12,357
We should start heading back now, or else
we won't make it to town before dark.

246
00:14:12,440 --> 00:14:13,270
You're right.

247
00:14:18,240 --> 00:14:22,400
Wait, do you remember which
tunnel we came in from?

248
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:29,077
We've been walking a long time.

249
00:14:29,160 --> 00:14:31,960
Is this the right tunnel,
or was it the other?

250
00:14:32,780 --> 00:14:33,610
Seriously?

251
00:14:33,720 --> 00:14:36,426
We picked this one because
you said we should.

252
00:14:36,720 --> 00:14:37,550
What?

253
00:14:37,633 --> 00:14:38,680
I didn't hear you.

254
00:14:38,960 --> 00:14:40,060
Uh, never mind.

255
00:14:41,680 --> 00:14:42,510
Shh.

256
00:14:48,120 --> 00:14:49,320
Is that the wind?

257
00:14:49,620 --> 00:14:51,149
You picked the right path.

258
00:14:51,440 --> 00:14:53,146
We're almost to the entrance.

259
00:14:53,840 --> 00:14:54,670
Wait!

260
00:14:54,753 --> 00:14:57,188
Be careful or you'll
trip and hurt yourself!

261
00:15:06,140 --> 00:15:07,260
There it is!

262
00:15:22,560 --> 00:15:23,920
Where are we?

263
00:15:24,740 --> 00:15:27,260
The dark territory.

264
00:15:29,940 --> 00:15:30,960
Oh, no.

265
00:15:31,460 --> 00:15:32,860
We better turn around.

266
00:15:44,220 --> 00:15:45,320
Dragon Knights!

267
00:15:45,800 --> 00:15:47,080
That white one.

268
00:15:48,260 --> 00:15:50,980
That's a real-life
Integrity Knight, isn't it?

269
00:15:52,240 --> 00:15:54,660
And the others from the Dark Territory.

270
00:16:21,980 --> 00:16:24,900
Oh, my God.

271
00:16:56,960 --> 00:16:58,000
No, wait!

272
00:17:11,600 --> 00:17:12,430
Alice!

273
00:17:23,760 --> 00:17:26,540
In Book 1, Chapter 3, Verse 11,

274
00:17:26,740 --> 00:17:31,564
the index says, None shall cross the End
Mountains that surround the human empire.

275
00:17:34,260 --> 00:17:35,090
Alice!

276
00:17:38,020 --> 00:17:39,180
What have I done?

277
00:17:39,500 --> 00:17:41,340
Don't worry, Alice. It's okay.

278
00:17:41,640 --> 00:17:43,757
I mean, it's not like you left the cave.

279
00:17:43,840 --> 00:17:44,780
You didn't.

280
00:17:44,980 --> 00:17:46,280
She didn't, did she?

281
00:17:47,200 --> 00:17:48,030
Kirito?

282
00:17:55,160 --> 00:17:56,020
What's that?

283
00:17:56,360 --> 00:17:58,560
A singular unit has been detected.

284
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:00,280
Tracing its ID.

285
00:18:01,160 --> 00:18:02,219
Coordinates fixed.

286
00:18:03,380 --> 00:18:04,580
Report complete.

287
00:18:08,460 --> 00:18:09,780
What was that thing?

288
00:18:10,180 --> 00:18:11,080
I don't know.

289
00:18:11,780 --> 00:18:13,074
Let's get out of here.

290
00:18:31,100 --> 00:18:34,480
So, guys, where are we going to put this?

291
00:18:38,040 --> 00:18:41,393
I'll put the ice in my basement
where it's nice and cool.

292
00:18:41,560 --> 00:18:42,940
Okay, see ya.

293
00:18:50,680 --> 00:18:54,940
I think tomorrow's lunch will
be the best one yet. Can't wait.

294
00:18:55,540 --> 00:18:56,520
Me neither.

295
00:19:20,320 --> 00:19:21,150
Alice...

296
00:19:26,060 --> 00:19:27,060
Don't go!

297
00:19:27,600 --> 00:19:28,540
Alice!

298
00:19:29,680 --> 00:19:31,080
Alice!

299
00:20:02,420 --> 00:20:05,220
I don't know.

300
00:20:06,860 --> 00:20:08,500
An Integrity Knight!

301
00:20:09,060 --> 00:20:11,920
Yeah, he's the same one from yesterday.

302
00:20:13,800 --> 00:20:15,220
Oh no, Alice.

303
00:20:15,800 --> 00:20:17,240
He's come for her.

304
00:20:17,840 --> 00:20:20,320
But he can't take her away for that!

305
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:23,080
Come on!

306
00:20:24,700 --> 00:20:25,540
Wait!

307
00:20:44,380 --> 00:20:45,210
Alice!

308
00:20:46,840 --> 00:20:49,180
Kirito! Yu-Gi-Oh! Keep it down.

309
00:20:50,120 --> 00:20:52,591
Better get out of here before he sees you.

310
00:20:58,760 --> 00:20:59,900
It's my father.

311
00:21:05,380 --> 00:21:09,240
I am Gosfut Zuburg, the
elder of this village.

312
00:21:11,620 --> 00:21:14,120
I am Deo Selbert Synthesis 7,

313
00:21:14,540 --> 00:21:18,677
the Axiom Integrity Knight who oversees
the northern Norlingarth territory.

314
00:21:18,760 --> 00:21:22,580
Your daughter, Alice Zuburg,
has disobeyed the taboo index.

315
00:21:23,120 --> 00:21:27,780
I shall take her with me to answer
for her crimes and be executed.

316
00:21:32,580 --> 00:21:33,680
Taboo Index,

317
00:21:33,980 --> 00:21:39,880
Book 1, Chapter 3, Verse 11 states, None
shall cross into the dark territory.

318
00:22:01,400 --> 00:22:02,230
Sir Knight!

319
00:22:04,380 --> 00:22:07,040
Alice never set foot
in the Dark Territory.

320
00:22:07,280 --> 00:22:08,398
It was an accident.

321
00:22:08,780 --> 00:22:10,721
All she did was touch the ground.

322
00:22:10,820 --> 00:22:12,291
It was only for a second.

323
00:22:12,720 --> 00:22:15,320
That is enough to charge
her with the crime.

324
00:22:16,100 --> 00:22:18,580
Then we're just as guilty as she is.

325
00:22:18,860 --> 00:22:20,600
We were right there with her.

326
00:22:20,860 --> 00:22:23,440
If you take her, then take us too.

327
00:22:27,500 --> 00:22:30,800
Yu-Gi-Oh, listen, I'm gonna
charge him with the axe.

328
00:22:31,440 --> 00:22:32,840
Grab Alice and run.

329
00:22:33,720 --> 00:22:36,260
Hold on, I don't, we can't.

330
00:22:36,440 --> 00:22:37,969
I don't care what happens.

331
00:22:38,280 --> 00:22:41,398
Her life's more important
than some stupid old rules.

332
00:23:01,640 --> 00:23:02,470
Kirito!

333
00:23:03,380 --> 00:23:05,851
Escort those two children from the square.

334
00:23:07,360 --> 00:23:08,400
Let her go!

335
00:23:18,540 --> 00:23:20,900
Don't just stand there! Go help her!

336
00:23:40,360 --> 00:23:43,080
U-U-Gio, get these guys off me!

337
00:23:43,360 --> 00:23:44,340
Come on, hurry!

338
00:23:44,780 --> 00:23:45,720
U-U-Gio!

339
00:23:53,800 --> 00:23:55,500
Oh, my God.

340
00:24:32,400 --> 00:24:34,440
Oh, my God.

341
00:25:00,120 --> 00:25:01,520
Let's go.

342
00:25:37,220 --> 00:25:39,360
This turning costume is full auto!

343
00:25:43,620 --> 00:25:45,540
What's up, you PK jerks?

344
00:25:45,860 --> 00:25:47,580
Let's see how fast you run!

345
00:26:04,160 --> 00:26:04,990
Cowards!

346
00:26:07,940 --> 00:26:09,260
You're up! I'll cover!

347
00:26:38,600 --> 00:26:40,380
Are those Photon Swords?

348
00:26:41,460 --> 00:26:42,757
Team A needs backup.

349
00:26:42,840 --> 00:26:44,800
B and C, head to Grid 4-6.

350
00:26:45,620 --> 00:26:48,400
You have permission to
use grenades. Hey, boss.

351
00:26:48,780 --> 00:26:50,000
Let me in on this.

352
00:26:50,300 --> 00:26:52,241
No, this op's about to wind down.

353
00:26:53,480 --> 00:26:55,040
Just sit back and watch.

354
00:27:17,200 --> 00:27:18,240
I got this!

355
00:27:43,440 --> 00:27:44,340
Damn it.

356
00:27:48,980 --> 00:27:50,686
Well, that's the end of that.

357
00:27:51,620 --> 00:27:52,880
All teams retreat.

358
00:27:53,880 --> 00:27:55,400
Grid 1-9's too hot.

359
00:27:58,820 --> 00:28:01,677
We could have killed them
all if we stuck with it.

360
00:28:01,760 --> 00:28:04,642
You sure you want to end
the day like this, boss?

361
00:28:05,480 --> 00:28:07,304
That team's all over the place.

362
00:28:07,680 --> 00:28:09,737
Fighting them won't
help with our training.

363
00:28:09,820 --> 00:28:13,349
We have the big mission coming
up and we need to stay sharp.

364
00:28:14,000 --> 00:28:14,830
Let's go.

365
00:28:19,720 --> 00:28:21,600
Till next time, kid.

366
00:28:26,720 --> 00:28:31,840
Oh, man, I heard GGO was going to
be hardcore, but that was insane.

367
00:28:32,260 --> 00:28:36,142
I never played a game where it's
cool just to run around and kill.

368
00:28:36,500 --> 00:28:39,757
Actually, there's a method
to the madness of PKing here.

369
00:28:39,840 --> 00:28:42,357
You go after other players
for their cashier items.

370
00:28:42,440 --> 00:28:45,793
But the team we just fought
didn't care about that stuff.

371
00:28:45,900 --> 00:28:49,657
Yeah, the only thing those guys
wanted was to straight up kill us.

372
00:28:49,740 --> 00:28:52,517
And did you see all the grenades
and smoke bombs they used?

373
00:28:52,600 --> 00:28:54,220
Isn't that stuff expensive?

374
00:28:54,640 --> 00:28:55,740
You know it.

375
00:28:55,940 --> 00:28:58,917
And that's how they fight
every single time they show up.

376
00:28:59,000 --> 00:29:03,297
They go after teams that are out in the
middle of nowhere, massacre everyone,

377
00:29:03,380 --> 00:29:05,615
then disappear without looting anyone.

378
00:29:05,780 --> 00:29:07,200
I saw their stats.

379
00:29:07,400 --> 00:29:09,217
Is it true they've never lost a battle?

380
00:29:09,300 --> 00:29:11,260
Yeah, it's true they haven't.

381
00:29:12,320 --> 00:29:15,417
Still, I thought if anyone
could beat them, we could.

382
00:29:15,500 --> 00:29:19,317
Because as a team, we're not like
anyone they've come up against yet.

383
00:29:19,400 --> 00:29:22,180
Oh well, I guess it just
wasn't in the cards.

384
00:29:22,700 --> 00:29:25,524
I didn't expect they'd
retreat, that's for sure.

385
00:29:25,620 --> 00:29:26,540
Hey, no biggie.

386
00:29:26,660 --> 00:29:27,954
It's not like we lost.

387
00:29:28,320 --> 00:29:31,340
Besides, they ran, so
that's a win in my book.

388
00:29:31,540 --> 00:29:36,011
The point was to find out who they were
and what they were up to, tough guy.

389
00:29:36,420 --> 00:29:38,580
Yeah, well, a win's a win.

390
00:29:39,520 --> 00:29:43,317
That said, it would have been nice
to find out the leader's name.

391
00:29:43,400 --> 00:29:47,871
Yeah, but with the way they fought, it
wasn't even clear who the leader was.

392
00:29:48,780 --> 00:29:50,340
Hey, don't flap on me.

393
00:29:50,600 --> 00:29:51,577
Oh, I look like a pillow.

394
00:29:51,660 --> 00:29:53,777
But he said he's been taking time off from

395
00:29:53,860 --> 00:29:56,448
school since Thursday
and touring companies.

396
00:29:56,700 --> 00:30:00,465
Knowing him, he's probably mixed
up in something sinister again.

397
00:30:03,040 --> 00:30:06,280
Thanks again for helping me
out, guys. You're the best.

398
00:30:07,440 --> 00:30:09,300
No problems. Anytime. Later.

399
00:30:10,420 --> 00:30:12,280
Today was fun. See ya.

400
00:30:13,400 --> 00:30:17,020
Well, bye. No, wait. One sec. What's up?

401
00:30:17,200 --> 00:30:20,137
I was hoping you guys could
help me with something.

402
00:30:20,220 --> 00:30:21,840
That squad of PKers?

403
00:30:22,060 --> 00:30:24,260
No, it's something else, actually.

404
00:30:27,300 --> 00:30:31,020
If you and Kirito have time,
could we meet IRL tomorrow?

405
00:30:31,540 --> 00:30:32,940
I think so.

406
00:30:33,660 --> 00:30:35,425
Yeah, I'm free in the evening.

407
00:30:35,520 --> 00:30:37,177
Do you want to meet at Aikyo's?

408
00:30:37,260 --> 00:30:38,090
Sure.

409
00:30:38,340 --> 00:30:42,900
Oh, I'll also email you the plan so
you can think about it, if that's okay.

410
00:30:43,480 --> 00:30:44,310
Sounds good.

411
00:30:51,440 --> 00:30:52,560
You're so thin.

412
00:30:52,880 --> 00:30:53,762
Are you eating?

413
00:30:53,960 --> 00:30:55,195
What are you, my mom?

414
00:30:57,100 --> 00:30:59,453
Anyway, what is it you wanted to ask me?

415
00:30:59,920 --> 00:31:02,260
Is it about B .O .B.? Mm-hmm.

416
00:31:03,220 --> 00:31:06,437
There's a player calling himself
Sutilizer who won B .O .B.

417
00:31:06,520 --> 00:31:07,350
4.

418
00:31:07,433 --> 00:31:10,040
He's the same guy who
won the first B .O .B.

419
00:31:10,760 --> 00:31:11,590
Huh.

420
00:31:12,180 --> 00:31:14,080
When we found out he was in 4,

421
00:31:14,420 --> 00:31:17,197
everyone got excited because
he's like a legend, you know?

422
00:31:17,280 --> 00:31:19,720
Yeah, we all watched the live feed.

423
00:31:20,200 --> 00:31:22,657
Can't believe he started
with just his bare hands.

424
00:31:22,740 --> 00:31:26,957
He fought with a confident, stealthy
style, like that team from the other day.

425
00:31:27,040 --> 00:31:29,452
They did have the same vibe, didn't they?

426
00:31:29,980 --> 00:31:33,700
Well, except subtilizers on a
whole other level than them.

427
00:31:35,300 --> 00:31:37,240
He killed me so fast.

428
00:31:37,580 --> 00:31:39,404
I didn't even have time to aim.

429
00:31:39,540 --> 00:31:42,197
That's how it was for
everyone in the tourney.

430
00:31:42,280 --> 00:31:44,751
It's like he knew our moves before we did.

431
00:31:45,020 --> 00:31:46,097
No way, really?

432
00:31:46,180 --> 00:31:47,010
Really?

433
00:31:47,093 --> 00:31:48,364
But you're all vets at B .O .B.

434
00:31:48,600 --> 00:31:51,600
How could he anticipate
everyone's moves like that?

435
00:31:51,840 --> 00:31:55,360
I suppose as vets there's a
predictability to how we play.

436
00:31:55,480 --> 00:31:58,304
We tend to use the same
moves because they work.

437
00:31:58,620 --> 00:32:00,679
Which brings me to why you're here.

438
00:32:02,780 --> 00:32:05,757
I was thinking that a player
with a more chaotic fighting

439
00:32:05,840 --> 00:32:09,487
style might have a better chance
at outmaneuvering Settilizer.

440
00:32:09,660 --> 00:32:12,200
Anyway, the point is, the next B .O .B.

441
00:32:12,340 --> 00:32:16,997
is going to be happening at the end of the
year, and I'd like you to sign up for it.

442
00:32:17,080 --> 00:32:17,997
Huh? Uh...

443
00:32:18,080 --> 00:32:21,697
There's no way I'm gonna let
myself lose to the same guy again.

444
00:32:21,780 --> 00:32:22,880
He's going down.

445
00:32:24,680 --> 00:32:26,680
Looks like you made some progress.

446
00:32:28,340 --> 00:32:29,377
Oh, yeah.

447
00:32:29,460 --> 00:32:33,342
I still get the shakes every now
and then, but I'm getting better.

448
00:32:34,300 --> 00:32:35,360
And your friend.

449
00:32:35,620 --> 00:32:36,973
Is he doing any better?

450
00:32:38,480 --> 00:32:39,900
You mean Shinkawa.

451
00:32:41,420 --> 00:32:43,380
Yeah, he's making progress.

452
00:32:44,080 --> 00:32:47,021
I'll probably go visit him
again in a couple days.

453
00:32:47,600 --> 00:32:48,430
That's good.

454
00:32:49,160 --> 00:32:51,280
Well, look on the bright side.

455
00:32:51,480 --> 00:32:53,397
He's finally getting the help he needs.

456
00:32:53,480 --> 00:32:54,480
Death Gun's over.

457
00:32:55,000 --> 00:32:56,180
No, it isn't.

458
00:32:56,340 --> 00:32:58,577
His partner's still out there, remember?

459
00:32:58,660 --> 00:33:02,680
Yeah, but Kikuoka said they'll
catch up with him soon enough.

460
00:33:02,900 --> 00:33:04,440
Yeah, I hope so.

461
00:33:05,860 --> 00:33:06,940
Sorry I'm late.

462
00:33:07,600 --> 00:33:08,857
Hey there, Shinanon.

463
00:33:08,940 --> 00:33:12,300
What'd you just call her?
Hey, Asuna. Right on time.

464
00:33:13,640 --> 00:33:16,420
I read your email about
B .O .B. 5. I'm in.

465
00:33:16,760 --> 00:33:19,360
Wait, you asked her to help, too? Yep.

466
00:33:19,640 --> 00:33:23,157
I figured if it were just you,
there's a chance you'd get to aggro.

467
00:33:23,240 --> 00:33:26,180
Even good dogs need a
leash, right? Tonkii.

468
00:33:26,760 --> 00:33:27,840
Hey, Kirito?

469
00:33:29,840 --> 00:33:30,777
You're so thin.

470
00:33:30,860 --> 00:33:31,780
Are you eating?

471
00:33:32,300 --> 00:33:33,300
Yeah, I am.

472
00:33:33,900 --> 00:33:34,730
Ha! See?

473
00:33:34,840 --> 00:33:36,637
She can even tell something's up.

474
00:33:36,720 --> 00:33:38,720
It's that part-time job, isn't it?

475
00:33:41,500 --> 00:33:42,330
Honestly.

476
00:33:42,413 --> 00:33:44,460
Physically, you're fine, so far.

477
00:33:46,460 --> 00:33:47,737
Wait, you can tell?

478
00:33:47,820 --> 00:33:48,800
What's that?

479
00:33:50,100 --> 00:33:52,140
It's exactly what it looks like.

480
00:33:52,700 --> 00:33:53,530
Huh?

481
00:33:53,613 --> 00:33:55,560
You mean she can track your vitals?

482
00:33:55,800 --> 00:33:56,660
Neat, huh?

483
00:33:57,080 --> 00:33:58,220
Yeah, I guess.

484
00:33:58,420 --> 00:33:59,900
But, like, how's it work?

485
00:34:00,320 --> 00:34:04,780
A little while ago, I had this
miniature sensor implanted in my chest.

486
00:34:05,360 --> 00:34:06,713
It sends my heart rate,

487
00:34:06,820 --> 00:34:10,677
body temperature, and other stuff
over the net to us in a smartphone.

488
00:34:10,760 --> 00:34:11,590
What?

489
00:34:11,673 --> 00:34:12,657
Why would you want to do...

490
00:34:12,740 --> 00:34:14,297
Oh, I get it.

491
00:34:14,380 --> 00:34:16,017
It's an anti-cheating system.

492
00:34:16,100 --> 00:34:17,360
No, not even.

493
00:34:18,260 --> 00:34:22,436
When I started this part-time job,
they thought it'd be good to get it.

494
00:34:22,720 --> 00:34:24,777
I have to wear electrodes
and sticking them

495
00:34:24,860 --> 00:34:27,297
on and pulling them off
is kind of a hassle.

496
00:34:27,380 --> 00:34:31,300
Using it like this was her idea,
so I made a little app for it.

497
00:34:31,800 --> 00:34:34,697
Yeah, something about looking
at it's kind of soothing.

498
00:34:34,780 --> 00:34:37,720
Knowing that's Kirito's heart beating.

499
00:34:38,560 --> 00:34:41,220
I get all woozy and my
head starts to spin.

500
00:34:43,580 --> 00:34:45,720
That's both cute and kind of creepy.

501
00:34:46,600 --> 00:34:50,541
Anyway, with you on my side, I'll
have a machine gun in my pillbox.

502
00:34:50,760 --> 00:34:52,600
You're exactly the edge I need.

503
00:34:53,100 --> 00:34:55,400
I'm happy to help any way I can.

504
00:34:56,720 --> 00:34:58,300
Now then. What?

505
00:34:58,640 --> 00:35:02,228
I want to hear some more about
this sketchy new job of yours.

506
00:35:02,440 --> 00:35:06,220
Let me guess, you're alpha
testing a new VR MMO game, right?

507
00:35:07,700 --> 00:35:09,620
Actually, it's not a game.

508
00:35:10,300 --> 00:35:14,771
It's a brain-machine interface designed
for this brand new full dive system.

509
00:35:15,840 --> 00:35:17,820
Rath developed it. They're new.

510
00:35:18,100 --> 00:35:20,276
What the heck kind of a name is Rath?

511
00:35:20,380 --> 00:35:22,437
It's the name of an imaginary creature.

512
00:35:22,520 --> 00:35:25,357
I remember it from the book
Through the Looking Glass.

513
00:35:25,440 --> 00:35:28,277
Some characters said it was
a pig and others a turtle.

514
00:35:28,360 --> 00:35:32,260
So, are they releasing some
next-gen full-dive rig for gaming?

515
00:35:33,800 --> 00:35:35,500
I don't know. Maybe.

516
00:35:36,160 --> 00:35:40,357
This thing's totally different compared
to the full-dive tech that's out now.

517
00:35:40,440 --> 00:35:41,270
Oh.

518
00:35:41,353 --> 00:35:43,660
So, what's the in-game world like?

519
00:35:44,620 --> 00:35:46,280
I have no idea.

520
00:35:47,040 --> 00:35:47,870
Huh?

521
00:35:47,953 --> 00:35:50,034
It's how they keep things confidential.

522
00:35:50,520 --> 00:35:54,040
The memories I make using
their rig in the VR world,

523
00:35:54,180 --> 00:35:56,709
they don't stick with
me in the real world.

524
00:35:57,180 --> 00:36:00,004
Whatever I saw during the
tests, whatever I did,

525
00:36:00,100 --> 00:36:02,580
I'd forget all of it after I log out.

526
00:36:03,720 --> 00:36:04,550
Huh?

527
00:36:04,633 --> 00:36:06,380
You can't remember anything at all?

528
00:36:06,660 --> 00:36:09,520
Oh my god, is it another Ogma?

529
00:36:12,120 --> 00:36:13,820
No, it's not like that.

530
00:36:14,060 --> 00:36:16,977
This rig doesn't put stress on
your brain like the Ogma did.

531
00:36:17,060 --> 00:36:22,001
I didn't lose my memories or anything, I
just can't access them from my Fluct light.

532
00:36:22,280 --> 00:36:23,780
A Fluct what?

533
00:36:24,860 --> 00:36:27,389
This is going to take
some time to explain.

534
00:36:28,620 --> 00:36:32,440
First off, the rig I'm testing
is called the Soul Translator.

535
00:36:34,620 --> 00:36:37,267
Where in your body do
you think your soul is?

536
00:36:38,140 --> 00:36:38,970
Seriously?

537
00:36:39,053 --> 00:36:39,883
I don't know.

538
00:36:39,966 --> 00:36:40,840
In the brain?

539
00:36:41,300 --> 00:36:44,888
If you zoom into the brain,
you'll see it's made up of cells.

540
00:36:45,400 --> 00:36:48,760
So, where in all those cells
do you think the soul is?

541
00:36:49,580 --> 00:36:50,437
I don't know.

542
00:36:50,520 --> 00:36:53,237
Zoom into a brain cell
and you'll see that it has

543
00:36:53,320 --> 00:36:55,637
things in it that support
the cell's structure.

544
00:36:55,720 --> 00:36:57,367
They're called microtubules.

545
00:36:57,900 --> 00:36:58,730
Okay.

546
00:36:59,040 --> 00:37:01,922
Like the name implies,
they're like hollow pipes.

547
00:37:02,040 --> 00:37:03,334
But they're not empty.

548
00:37:03,460 --> 00:37:05,401
They got something sealed inside.

549
00:37:06,400 --> 00:37:08,380
So, what do they have inside?

550
00:37:09,360 --> 00:37:10,190
Light.

551
00:37:11,040 --> 00:37:11,870
That's it.

552
00:37:12,340 --> 00:37:13,399
Fluctuating light.

553
00:37:13,960 --> 00:37:17,700
It's the building block of the
human soul, according to Rath.

554
00:37:17,840 --> 00:37:19,617
So let me see if I understand this.

555
00:37:19,700 --> 00:37:22,420
They're saying this light in brain cells.

556
00:37:22,680 --> 00:37:24,780
That's the soul? Yeah.

557
00:37:25,340 --> 00:37:27,717
They don't call it a
soul at Wrath, though.

558
00:37:27,800 --> 00:37:32,480
They decided to go with a combination
of the words fluctuating and light.

559
00:37:33,300 --> 00:37:34,535
Fluctlight for short.

560
00:37:35,680 --> 00:37:39,137
And the Soul Translator doesn't
just read a person's brain,

561
00:37:39,220 --> 00:37:40,749
it reads their Fluctlight.

562
00:37:40,940 --> 00:37:44,400
Which means it can also
imprint on them. Imprint?

563
00:37:44,780 --> 00:37:45,877
Like the atmosphere.

564
00:37:45,960 --> 00:37:49,160
That rig lets you experience
VR by sending images,

565
00:37:49,440 --> 00:37:52,499
sounds, and other sensory
information to your brain.

566
00:37:52,660 --> 00:37:53,720
With this rig,

567
00:37:53,960 --> 00:37:58,317
since it's next-gen and all, it would
work the same way but on your soul, right?

568
00:37:58,400 --> 00:37:59,600
Yeah, that's right.

569
00:38:00,140 --> 00:38:02,081
The name pretty much says it all.

570
00:38:02,400 --> 00:38:04,760
The Soul Translator, or STL,

571
00:38:04,980 --> 00:38:07,057
writes short-term memories
onto your Fluctlight

572
00:38:07,140 --> 00:38:10,199
of the sights and sounds
it wants you to experience.

573
00:38:11,360 --> 00:38:13,577
Mnemonic visual data is what it's called.

574
00:38:13,660 --> 00:38:17,460
I remember the test dives I took
at the beginning of the job.

575
00:38:19,440 --> 00:38:21,028
Those dives were different.

576
00:38:21,280 --> 00:38:22,660
I was blown away.

577
00:38:23,500 --> 00:38:26,206
It's nothing like what
the Amusphere creates.

578
00:38:27,280 --> 00:38:31,515
Everything was so real, I couldn't
tell it was a virtual world at first.

579
00:38:31,820 --> 00:38:32,740
I don't know.

580
00:38:33,020 --> 00:38:34,140
This scares me.

581
00:38:35,040 --> 00:38:37,580
I mean, is it safe?

582
00:38:38,140 --> 00:38:38,970
Mr.

583
00:38:39,053 --> 00:38:43,664
Kikuoka offered you the job, and that's
great, but who knows what his motives are.

584
00:38:43,960 --> 00:38:47,842
Yeah, you're right, but I don't
let my guard down around him ever.

585
00:38:48,320 --> 00:38:51,000
The thing is, I want to know.

586
00:38:51,660 --> 00:38:55,100
I have to do this to see
where full dive's heading.

587
00:38:55,500 --> 00:38:58,880
I know it's risky, but the STL's special.

588
00:38:59,580 --> 00:39:04,640
Sure, terms like mnemonic and flukplight
sound creepy, but I connect with it.

589
00:39:04,960 --> 00:39:06,666
Way more than the atmosphere.

590
00:39:06,800 --> 00:39:10,617
It's like a waking dream
when I'm in it. How so?

591
00:39:10,700 --> 00:39:14,000
You know how you sometimes
have dreams that seem long?

592
00:39:14,400 --> 00:39:18,297
The kind where you wake up and you'd
swear that dream went on for hours,

593
00:39:18,380 --> 00:39:20,321
especially if it was a nightmare?

594
00:39:20,580 --> 00:39:24,380
The truth is, that dream probably
only lasted a few minutes.

595
00:39:24,800 --> 00:39:29,220
You get that same phenomena if
you dive with the STL. Seriously?

596
00:39:29,940 --> 00:39:34,057
It's just like a dream that felt like
hours but was only a few minutes.

597
00:39:34,140 --> 00:39:38,420
Your time diving with the STL
is way longer than your dive.

598
00:39:39,840 --> 00:39:42,060
That's the main feature of the STL.

599
00:39:42,600 --> 00:39:47,120
Wrath calls it Fluctlight
Acceleration, or FLA for short.

600
00:39:48,460 --> 00:39:49,290
Whoa.

601
00:39:49,680 --> 00:39:50,920
I'm so confused.

602
00:39:51,200 --> 00:39:52,360
My head's spinning.

603
00:39:52,980 --> 00:39:57,380
You were diving for three whole days,
so how much time was that in VR?

604
00:39:58,160 --> 00:39:59,220
I'm not sure.

605
00:39:59,540 --> 00:40:01,834
It could have been ten days or a month.

606
00:40:02,100 --> 00:40:03,840
I don't remember how long.

607
00:40:04,700 --> 00:40:06,957
When I asked how long,
they wouldn't tell me.

608
00:40:07,040 --> 00:40:09,957
But they did tell me the
codename of the test world.

609
00:40:10,040 --> 00:40:10,870
Really?

610
00:40:10,953 --> 00:40:11,880
What is it?

611
00:40:12,320 --> 00:40:13,280
The Underworld.

612
00:40:13,500 --> 00:40:16,840
So it's like an underground
world? It's a reference.

613
00:40:17,300 --> 00:40:19,620
It has to do with Alice, same as Raph.

614
00:40:20,100 --> 00:40:22,857
Alice in Wonderland was the title
the book was published under,

615
00:40:22,940 --> 00:40:26,175
but it had a different title
when it was being written.

616
00:40:26,420 --> 00:40:29,773
Originally, it was called
Alice's Adventures Underground.

617
00:40:31,000 --> 00:40:31,840
You okay?

618
00:40:33,020 --> 00:40:37,880
When I heard the name Alice, it felt
like I was about to remember something.

619
00:40:38,380 --> 00:40:39,860
Something about the test?

620
00:40:40,120 --> 00:40:41,320
I'm not sure.

621
00:40:41,800 --> 00:40:44,460
It feels like there's
something I need to do.

622
00:40:44,760 --> 00:40:46,700
I just can't remember what.

623
00:40:50,520 --> 00:40:52,560
Thanks, Egil. See you later.

624
00:40:53,120 --> 00:40:53,950
Bye, guys.

625
00:41:00,360 --> 00:41:02,948
I'll keep you guys up
to date about B .O .B.

626
00:41:03,240 --> 00:41:05,577
Thanks again for meeting up with me today.

627
00:41:05,660 --> 00:41:06,490
Sure.

628
00:41:06,573 --> 00:41:07,717
See you later, Sheenanone.

629
00:41:07,800 --> 00:41:08,630
See ya.

630
00:41:10,280 --> 00:41:11,300
That was fun.

631
00:41:13,140 --> 00:41:14,840
What's wrong? Say what?

632
00:41:15,920 --> 00:41:17,080
Oh, nothing.

633
00:41:34,720 --> 00:41:35,840
Talk to me.

634
00:41:39,500 --> 00:41:40,330
Asuna.

635
00:41:42,060 --> 00:41:44,800
I think I'm gonna go.

636
00:41:45,120 --> 00:41:46,880
To America? Yeah.

637
00:41:47,580 --> 00:41:50,180
The research is way more advanced there.

638
00:41:50,420 --> 00:41:51,832
It's all next-gen stuff.

639
00:41:52,380 --> 00:41:57,080
They're creating a new world, and
I want to be there when it's born.

640
00:41:59,220 --> 00:42:04,500
We were happy in Aincrad, but there
was so much pain and sadness, too.

641
00:42:05,080 --> 00:42:08,197
You want to find out why that
castle still haunts your thoughts,

642
00:42:08,280 --> 00:42:10,920
and where that experience is taking you.

643
00:42:11,320 --> 00:42:15,520
Even if I lived a couple hundred
years, I doubt I'd ever find that out.

644
00:42:17,440 --> 00:42:19,380
Anyway, I want...

645
00:42:20,740 --> 00:42:23,720
I want you with me, Asuna. Always.

646
00:42:24,640 --> 00:42:27,117
I want you to come with me, and I...

647
00:42:27,200 --> 00:42:30,797
I know that's asking a
lot, but the truth is...

648
00:42:30,880 --> 00:42:33,480
I can't do this without you!

649
00:42:39,720 --> 00:42:42,380
Of course, I'll go anywhere with you.

650
00:42:42,980 --> 00:42:44,520
It doesn't matter where.

651
00:42:45,180 --> 00:42:46,010
I'll go.

652
00:42:46,880 --> 00:42:47,710
Asuna.

653
00:42:59,260 --> 00:43:03,025
So does this mean the Soul
Translator isn't the next step in VR?

654
00:43:03,680 --> 00:43:06,268
Hearing you talk about
it, I thought it was.

655
00:43:07,980 --> 00:43:09,040
I don't know.

656
00:43:09,640 --> 00:43:14,780
For some reason, I get the feeling its
purpose isn't just a full dive in VR worlds.

657
00:43:15,140 --> 00:43:16,460
Then what's it for?

658
00:43:16,740 --> 00:43:20,387
A tool for learning about
Fluctlights and human consciousness.

659
00:43:22,900 --> 00:43:23,780
It's like,

660
00:43:24,020 --> 00:43:27,117
whatever I know about
the STL makes me think

661
00:43:27,200 --> 00:43:29,740
it might be an extension
of Kayaba's ideas.

662
00:43:31,040 --> 00:43:32,160
He's behind it?

663
00:43:32,380 --> 00:43:34,877
I don't know why he made the NerveGear and

664
00:43:34,960 --> 00:43:38,237
SAO to trap everyone
and make us all suffer.

665
00:43:38,320 --> 00:43:40,660
Or why he'd fry his own brain.

666
00:43:40,920 --> 00:43:41,940
And the seed.

667
00:43:42,120 --> 00:43:44,780
He didn't make it just
to keep Fairy alive.

668
00:43:46,260 --> 00:43:48,337
I want to know what his endgame was.

669
00:43:48,420 --> 00:43:50,244
But I don't want it to be mine.

670
00:43:50,940 --> 00:43:52,080
I'm not his puppet.

671
00:43:52,280 --> 00:43:54,620
And if I go down that road, I would be.

672
00:43:54,880 --> 00:43:56,397
You said you talked to him.

673
00:43:56,480 --> 00:43:59,240
Or the part of him he left behind. Yeah.

674
00:44:00,480 --> 00:44:03,715
I think I know why he left
a copy of himself out there.

675
00:44:03,800 --> 00:44:07,976
And it might have something to do
with what Wrath's up to with the STL.

676
00:44:10,600 --> 00:44:12,460
Hey, sorry to bother you.

677
00:44:13,140 --> 00:44:14,380
I'm sort of lost.

678
00:44:14,680 --> 00:44:15,856
Where's the station?

679
00:44:16,120 --> 00:44:17,520
Oh, just down there.

680
00:44:19,760 --> 00:44:20,590
Kirito?

681
00:44:21,560 --> 00:44:23,760
You followed us from Dicey's cafe.

682
00:44:25,600 --> 00:44:27,860
There goes my plan to ambush y 'all.

683
00:44:28,260 --> 00:44:29,100
Who are you?

684
00:44:29,320 --> 00:44:30,880
Oh, come on, Kirito.

685
00:44:31,120 --> 00:44:32,473
Don't you recognize me?

686
00:44:32,840 --> 00:44:34,477
Oh, that's right.

687
00:44:34,560 --> 00:44:36,460
I always wore a mask back there.

688
00:44:37,720 --> 00:44:42,720
Yeah, now that Zaza's been caught, there's
no one left to finish things but me.

689
00:44:43,400 --> 00:44:46,300
The last survivor of Laughing Coffin.

690
00:44:48,580 --> 00:44:49,860
Johnny Black.

691
00:44:56,980 --> 00:44:58,140
You ass!

692
00:44:58,380 --> 00:45:00,080
You got no sword here!

693
00:45:00,360 --> 00:45:02,900
So, you're still on the run?

694
00:45:03,120 --> 00:45:04,060
Of course!

695
00:45:04,900 --> 00:45:06,280
Damn, Kirito.

696
00:45:06,980 --> 00:45:10,940
I can't believe you're the same
dude that beat the hell out of us!

697
00:45:11,160 --> 00:45:13,572
But you're just a punk-ass kid, ain't ya?

698
00:45:13,800 --> 00:45:16,360
Take away your swords, and you're nothing.

699
00:45:17,280 --> 00:45:18,110
What about you?

700
00:45:18,193 --> 00:45:20,000
You don't have your poison dagger.

701
00:45:20,640 --> 00:45:21,760
I don't.

702
00:45:22,100 --> 00:45:24,620
You sure about that, Kirito?

703
00:45:25,820 --> 00:45:26,800
Death gun!

704
00:45:34,920 --> 00:45:36,280
Run! Get out of here!

705
00:46:02,600 --> 00:46:03,430
Kirito!

706
00:46:05,200 --> 00:46:06,160
Kirito

707
00:46:26,140 --> 00:46:26,970
beginning

708
00:46:59,900 --> 00:47:02,440
SHINING SOMER DIAMOND

709
00:47:35,720 --> 00:47:38,240
Next time, the Demon Tree.
